  "worked_solution": "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\u27e8-4,\\,-5,\\,1\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e84,\\,5,\\,-1\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, applying the vector addition rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)+\u27e82,\\,1,\\,3\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{0}^{2}\u27e82,\\,1,\\,3\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\u27e84,\\,5,\\,-1\u27e9+{\u27e82t,\\,t,\\,3t\u27e9|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\u27e84,\\,5,\\,-1\u27e9+\u27e84,\\,2,\\,6\u27e9\\text{\u00a0} \\\\  & =\u27e88,\\,7,\\,5\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
